<section class="section section-alt">
  <div class="container article-body" style="max-width:920px;">
    <h2>The 10-Inch Round — Capacity, Value, and Event Planning</h2>
    <p>Serving up to 16 guests with ease, the 10-inch round bridges the gap between intimate family dinners and large banquets. Starting at $32.99+, it costs roughly $2.00 to $2.75 per serving—significantly more economical than purchasing individual sundae treats or mini Blizzards for an entire gathering. Positioned directly between the compact <a href="/items/dq-cake-round-8inch">8-Inch Round ($22.99+)</a> and the sprawling <a href="/items/dq-sheet-cake">DQ Sheet Cake ($44.99+)</a>, it guarantees every attendee enjoys the iconic chocolate fudge crunch center.</p>

    <h2>DQ Cake Size Guide</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table">
      <thead><tr><th>DQ Cake</th><th>Price</th><th>Serves</th><th>Best For</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>8-inch Round</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$22.99+</td><td>8–10</td><td>Small gatherings, household birthday</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>10-inch Round</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$32.99+</td><td>12–16</td><td>Medium celebrations, most popular size</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong><a href="/items/oreo-blizzard-cake">Oreo® Blizzard® Cake (10-inch)</a></strong></td><td class="price-cell">$38.74+</td><td>12–16</td><td>Same size, Oreo pieces throughout</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong><a href="/items/dq-sheet-cake">Sheet Cake</a></strong></td><td class="price-cell">$44.99+</td><td>24–32</td><td>Large events, offices, group parties</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>

    <h2>Classic 10-Inch vs. Blizzard Cake Upgrades: Which Should You Pick?</h2>
    <p>While the Classic 10-Inch ($32.99+) relies on timeless vanilla and chocolate soft serve balanced by the chocolate fudge crunch core, the specialty <a href="/items/oreo-blizzard-cake">Oreo Blizzard Cake</a> ($38.74+) incorporates real crushed Oreo cookies directly into the upper soft serve tier. If your guest of honor is a devoted cookies-and-cream lover, the $5.75 upgrade delivers unbeatable texture and celebration appeal. For groups with varied preferences, the Classic remains an infallible, universally beloved staple.</p>

    <h2>Essential Pickup, Storage &amp; Defrosting Advice</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Advance Notice:</strong> Place custom decorated cake orders at least 48 hours beforehand—give extra lead time during May/June graduation rushes and December holidays.</li>
      <li><strong>Freezer Dimensions:</strong> Ensure you clear a 12x12 inch level shelf in your home freezer; an ice cream cake must remain flat to maintain decorative border stability.</li>
      <li><strong>Transport Readiness:</strong> Pick up your cake in an air-conditioned vehicle during warm months, or bring an insulated thermal bag or cooler for drives over 15 minutes.</li>
      <li><strong>The 10-Minute Tempering Rule:</strong> Let the cake sit at room temperature for 8 to 12 minutes before serving; this softens the outer frosting layer and allows your knife to slice smoothly through the frozen fudge crunch layer without cracking the cake.</li>
    </ul>

